    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Drumright sprang up nearly overnight in 1912 after a wildcatter struck oil, leading to a massive rush of speculators and workers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drumright%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early oil workers in Drumright lived in tents or boxcar shacks, leading the community to be known locally as Ragtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drumright%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Drumright Field produced more oil than any other field in the world by 1917.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
